#: src/project-panel.md:3
msgid "Project Panel"
msgstr "專案面板"

#: src/project-panel.md:5
msgid ""
"The project panel shows a tree view of your workspace's files and "
"directories. Toggle it with <code class=\"hljs\">project panel: toggle "
"focus</code> (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-shift-e\\|ctrl-shift-e</kbd>), "
"or click the **Project Panel** button in the status bar."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:9
msgid "![Project Panel](https://images.zed.dev/docs/project-panel/panel.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:11
msgid "Navigating"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:13
msgid ""
"Use the arrow keys to move through entries. <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">right\\|right</kbd> expands a directory and <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">left\\|left</kbd> collapses it. <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-left\\|ctrl-left</kbd> collapses every directory at "
"once. Press <kbd class=\"keybinding\">space\\|space</kbd> or click to "
"preview a selected file, without giving it a permanent tab. Editing the file "
"or double-clicking it promotes it to a permanent tab."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:16
msgid "Auto-reveal"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:18
msgid ""
"By default, switching files in the editor will automatically highlight it in "
"the project panel and scroll it into view. This can be disabled with the "
"`project_panel.auto_reveal_entries` setting."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:22
msgid "Sticky Scroll"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:24
msgid ""
"When `project_panel.sticky_scroll` is enabled (the default), ancestor "
"directories pin themselves to the top of the panel as you scroll, so you "
"always know which directory you're on."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:27
msgid ""
"![Project Panel: Sticky Scroll Enabled](https://images.zed.dev/docs/project-"
"panel/sticky-scroll-true.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:29
msgid ""
"![Project Panel: Sticky Scroll Disabled](https://images.zed.dev/docs/project-"
"panel/sticky-scroll-false.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:31
msgid "Directory Folding"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:33
msgid ""
"When `project_panel.auto_fold_dirs` is enabled (the default), chains of "
"directories that each contain a single child directory are collapsed into "
"one row (for example, `src/utils/helpers` instead of three separate levels). "
"Right-click a folded directory and choose **Unfold Directory** to expand the "
"chain, or **Fold Directory** to collapse it again."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:39
msgid ""
"![Project Panel: Auto Fold Directories Enabled](https://images.zed.dev/docs/"
"project-panel/auto-fold-dirs-true.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:41
msgid ""
"![Project Panel: Auto Fold Directories Disabled](https://images.zed.dev/docs/"
"project-panel/auto-fold-dirs-false.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:43
msgid "Selecting Multiple Entries"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:45
msgid ""
"Hold `shift` while pressing the up/down arrow keys to mark additional "
"entries. Most file operations, like cut, copy, trash, delete and drag, apply "
"to the full set of marked entries."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:49
msgid ""
"When exactly two files are marked, <code class=\"hljs\">project panel: "
"compare marked files</code> (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">alt-d\\|alt-d</kbd>) "
"opens a diff view comparing them."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:52
msgid ""
"![Project Panel: Compare Marked Files](https://images.zed.dev/docs/project-"
"panel/compare-marked-files.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:54
msgid "File Operations"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:56
msgid ""
"Right-click an entry to see the full list of available operations, or use "
"the keybindings below."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:59
msgid "Creating Files and Directories"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:61
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: new file</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-n\\|ctrl-n</kbd>) creates a new file inside the "
"selected directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:63
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: new directory</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">alt-cmd-n\\|alt-ctrl-n</kbd>) creates a new directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:66
msgid ""
"An inline editor appears so you can type the name. Press `enter` to confirm "
"or `escape` to cancel."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:69
msgid "Renaming"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:71
msgid ""
"Press <kbd class=\"keybinding\">f2\\|f2</kbd> to rename the selected entry. "
"The filename stem is pre-selected so you can type a new name without "
"accidentally changing the extension. Press `enter` to confirm or `escape` to "
"cancel."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:76
msgid "Cut, Copy, and Paste"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:78
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: cut</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-x\\|ctrl-x</kbd>) marks entries for moving."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:80
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: copy</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-c\\|ctrl-c</kbd>) marks entries for copying."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:82
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: paste</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-v\\|ctrl-v</kbd>) places them in the selected "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:85
msgid ""
"When pasting would create a name conflict, Zed appends a \"copy\" suffix (e."
"g., `file copy.txt`, `file copy 2.txt`). If a single file is pasted with a "
"generated suffix, the rename editor opens automatically so you can adjust "
"the name."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:89
msgid "Duplicate"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:91
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: duplicate</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-d\\|</kbd>) copies and pastes the selected entries "
"in one step."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:94
msgid "Trash and Delete"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:96
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: trash</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-backspace\\|delete</kbd>) moves entries to the "
"system trash."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:98
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: delete</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-backspace\\|ctrl-delete</kbd>) permanently "
"deletes entries."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:101
msgid ""
"Both actions show a confirmation prompt listing the affected files. If any "
"of the files have unsaved changes, the prompt warns you."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:104
msgid "Drag and Drop"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:106
msgid ""
"Drag entries within the panel to move them. Hold `alt` while dropping to "
"copy instead of move. You can also drag files from your operating system's "
"file manager into the project panel to copy them into the project. Drag and "
"drop can be disabled with the `project_panel.drag_and_drop` setting."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:111
msgid "Git Integration"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:113
msgid ""
"When `project_panel.git_status` is enabled (the default), file and directory "
"names are tinted to reflect their git status—modified, added, deleted, "
"untracked, or conflicting."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:116
msgid ""
"Setting `project_panel.git_status_indicator` to `true` (disabled by default) "
"adds a letter badge next to each name: **M** (modified), **A** (added), "
"**D** (deleted), **U** (untracked) or **!** (conflict)."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:120
msgid ""
"![Project Panel: Git Integration](https://images.zed.dev/docs/project-panel/"
"git-status.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:122
msgid ""
"Use <code class=\"hljs\">project panel: select next git entry</code> and "
"{#action project_panel::SelectPrevGitEntry} to jump between tracked files "
"with uncommitted changes. The right-click menu also offers **Restore File** "
"to discard changes and **View File History** to browse a file's commit log."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:127
msgid "Diagnostics"
msgstr "診斷"

#: src/project-panel.md:129
msgid ""
"The `project_panel.show_diagnostics` setting controls whether error and "
"warning indicators appear on file and folder icons. Set it to `\"all\"` to "
"see both errors and warnings, `\"errors\"` for errors only, or `\"off\"` to "
"hide them. Diagnostics propagate upward—if a file deep in a directory has an "
"error, its ancestor folders show an indicator too."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:135
msgid ""
"Enable `project_panel.diagnostic_badges` (disabled by default) to display "
"numeric error and warning counts next to each entry. Use <code "
"class=\"hljs\">project panel: select next diagnostic</code> and <code "
"class=\"hljs\">project panel: select prev diagnostic</code> to navigate "
"between files that have diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:140
msgid ""
"See also [Diagnostics & Quick Fixes](./diagnostics.md) for editor and tab "
"diagnostic settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:142
msgid "Filtering and Sorting"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:144
msgid "Hiding Files"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:146
msgid ""
"`project_panel.hide_gitignore` hides files matched by `.gitignore`. Toggle "
"this with <code class=\"hljs\">project panel: toggle hide git ignore</code>."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:148
msgid ""
"`project_panel.hide_hidden` hides dotfiles and other hidden entries. Toggle "
"with <code class=\"hljs\">project panel: toggle hide hidden</code>."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:151
msgid "Sorting"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:153
msgid "The `project_panel.sort_mode` setting controls grouping:"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:155
msgid ""
"`\"directories_first\"` (default) — directories appear before files at each "
"level."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:157
msgid "`\"files_first\"` — files appear before directories."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:158
msgid "`\"mixed\"` — directories and files are sorted together."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:160
msgid "The `project_panel.sort_order` setting controls name comparison:"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:162
msgid ""
"`\"default\"` — case-insensitive natural sort (`file2` before `file10`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:163
msgid "`\"upper\"` — uppercase names grouped first, then lowercase."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:164
msgid "`\"lower\"` — lowercase names grouped first, then uppercase."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:165
msgid "`\"unicode\"` — raw Unicode codepoint order with no case folding."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:167
msgid "Other Actions"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:169
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: reveal in file manager</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">alt-cmd-r\\|alt-ctrl-r</kbd>) reveals the selected "
"entry in Finder / File Explorer."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:171
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: new search in directory</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-shift-f\\|ctrl-alt-shift-f</kbd>) opens a "
"project search scoped to the selected directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:173
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: remove from project</code> removes a "
"workspace root folder from the project."
msgstr ""
